From: TDVP Platform <platform@tdvp.invalid>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 15:30:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] tdvp: select PulseAudio without user systemd

The TDVP desktop image starts a per-session PulseAudio daemon directly.  It
does not run a user systemd manager or ship PipeWire.  Upstream's runtime
PipeWire probe runs `systemctl --user`, which asks the system D-Bus daemon to
activate org.freedesktop.systemd1 and produces a misleading startup failure on
every panel launch.

Use the image's fixed audio contract instead of probing a service manager that
is intentionally absent.  This leaves the widget's PulseAudio control path and
the PulseAudio Bluetooth profile names selected by bluetooth.c intact.

The patch is deliberately platform-specific: remove it if TDVP changes its
audio stack to PipeWire and provides a functioning user systemd session.

Signed-off-by: TDVP Platform <platform@tdvp.invalid>
---
 src/volumepulse.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/volumepulse.c b/src/volumepulse.c
index c9f7594..5ad0c02 100644
--- a/src/volumepulse.c
+++ b/src/volumepulse.c
@@ -147,8 +147,11 @@ void hdmi_make_generic (VolumePulsePlugin *vol)
 gboolean check_pipewire (gpointer data)
 {
     VolumePulsePlugin *vol = (VolumePulsePlugin *) data;
-    if (!system ("systemctl --user -q is-active pipewire-pulse.service")) vol->pipewire = 1;
-    else vol->pipewire = 0;
+
+    /* TDVP starts PulseAudio itself and intentionally has no user systemd. */
+    vol->pipewire = 0;
+
+    /* Keep the existing log and the PulseAudio Bluetooth profile selection. */
 
     if (vol->pipewire)
     {
